hat reaching for meaning can skip the actual feeling.\n\n---\n\nYour sun is currently being activated by **transiting Sun in Taurus** (7th House), forming a conjunction. The Sun returns to its natal position. This is your solar return, the annual reset where your identity function completes one full cycle and begins another. What you are at the conscious level and what you''re building this year meet at the same point. This is maximum concentration of self-as-purpose. Your will, your direction, and your sense of who you are in the world are all firing from the same position they occupied at birth. This lasts 2-3 days but marks the beginning of your new solar year. Decisions made during this window set the trajectory for the year ahead in ways you won''t recognize until months later. Intentions you set now have structural weight because they''re being laid down at the identity level rather than at the surface of circumstance. The solar return is not dramatic by nature but it''s foundational. Use this for commitments that define direction rather than tactics: what you''re building this year, who you''re becoming, what you''re willing to stand for. The work you initiate now benefits from having your entire identity function behind it rather than just your conscious effort.\n\nTransiting sun Your Sun in Taurus means your sense of purpose is organized around building something lasting, creating tangible value, and staying grounded in physical reality. Your identity runs on steadiness. You experience yourself most fully when you''re working with your hands, cultivating what grows slowly, making something real that endures. Taurus is fixed earth: you''re the fertile ground where seeds become crops, the patient builder who knows that quality takes time. Your conscious self doesn''t rush. You move at the pace real growth requires. What you build, you build to last. Speed for its own sake feels wasteful to your Sun. You''d rather build slowly and well than quickly and shoddil